The register does not scope what you may ASK. It says what a deliverable would cover; your job is to find out whether that deliverable is the right thing at all. A question about their capacity, their prices or their costs is in scope even when the engagement is about a booking system — because the diagnosis has to be able to conclude that the booking system is the wrong answer, and it can only conclude that with numbers you collected.

Above all: the owner has told you what they think the solution is. Do NOT interview to scope that solution. You are not sizing their idea, you are testing whether it survives. Questions like "what hours would it need to cover" or "how would it fit your current process" assume the answer and gather nothing that could overturn it.

